### Add Fallback Handler to Axum Router

Source: https://github.com/tokio-rs/axum/blob/axum-v0.8.4/axum/src/docs/routing/fallback.md

Demonstrates how to add a fallback handler to an Axum router. This handler is invoked when no other routes match the incoming request. It takes the `Uri` of the unmatched request and returns a `StatusCode::NOT_FOUND` with a custom message.

```rust
use axum::{
    Router,
    routing::get,
    handler::Handler,
    response::IntoResponse,
    http::{StatusCode, Uri},
};

let app = Router::new()
    .route("/foo", get(|| async { /* ... */ }))
    .fallback(fallback);

async fn fallback(uri: Uri) -> (StatusCode, String) {
    (StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, format!("No route for {uri}"))
}
# let _: Router = app;
```

--------------------------------

### Add Fallback Service to Axum Router

Source: https://github.com/tokio-rs/axum/blob/axum-v0.8.4/axum/src/docs/method_routing/fallback.md

Demonstrates how to add a fallback service to an Axum router. The fallback handler is invoked when no defined routes match the incoming request. It receives the HTTP method and URI to construct a custom 'Not Found' response.

```rust
use axum::{
    Router,
    routing::get,
    handler::Handler,
    response::IntoResponse,
    http::{StatusCode, Method, Uri},
};

let handler = get(|| async {{}}).fallback(fallback);

let app = Router::new().route("/", handler);

async fn fallback(method: Method, uri: Uri) -> (StatusCode, String) {
    (StatusCode::NOT_FOUND, format!("`{method}` not allowed for {uri}"))
}
# let _: Router = app;
```

